\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p><strong>A new </strong><a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-Midyear.pdf\"><strong>mid-year crime report</strong></a> <strong>delivers more clear proof: President Donald J. Trump’s law-and-order agenda is crushing violent crime across America.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>According to the Major Cities Chiefs Association, homicides in the nation’s largest cities are down 17.2% from the first half of last year — alongside sharp declines in robberies, rapes, aggravated assaults, and overall violent crime. That translates to nearly 14,200 fewer reported violent crimes in just six months.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://www.axios.com/2026/08/11/big-city-homicides-decline-2026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\" noreferrer noopener\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"599\" height=\"617\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/major-chiefs-crime-midyear-chart.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-48001\" style=\"aspect-ratio:0.9708525234307063;object-fit:cover;width:500px\" srcset=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/major-chiefs-crime-midyear-chart.jpg 599w, https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/major-chiefs-crime-midyear-chart.jpg?resize=582,600 582w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 599px) 100vw, 599px\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>The results are especially striking in Democrat-run cities where the Trump Administration has aggressively surged federal resources and National Guard support after years of soft-on-crime failure. </strong>In Washington, D.C., homicides are down 43.9%. In Memphis, homicides are down 43.7%. In New Orleans, homicides are down nearly 25%.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This builds directly on last year’s already <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/01/icymi-murder-rate-plunges-to-125-year-low-as-president-trump-restores-law-and-order/\">historic</a> <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/02/icymi-violent-crime-plummets-across-major-u-s-cities/\">progress</a>, when murders and other violent crime plummeted to levels not seen in more than a century — and is the latest in a mountain of data all pointing to the same unmistakable reality. The Council on Criminal Justice <a href=\"https://counciloncj.org/homicide-likely-reaching-a-new-historic-low-as-most-crime-rates-continue-to-decline-at-mid-year/\">finds</a> the national murder rate is on pace to hit the lowest level in at least 126 years, while crime data analyst Jeff Asher <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2086810228998213731\">reports</a> the 2026 murder rate is tracking to be “by far the lowest ever recorded.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>This is the Trump Effect in full force.</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/08/icymi-violent-crime-keeps-falling-in-biggest-u-s-cities/\">ICYMI: “Violent crime keeps falling in biggest U.S. cities”</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
